1
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:58,390
Why not call it the Big Chill? Or the Nippy era?

2
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:01,390
I'm just saying how do we know it's an ice age?

3
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:04,310
Because of all the ice!

4
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:09,200
Well, things just got a little chillier.

5
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:12,650
Help! Help!

6
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:16,150
Come on, kids, let's go.
The traffic's moving.

7
00:04:16,490 --> 00:04:17,780
But, but, but dad.

8
00:04:18,490 --> 00:04:21,330
No "buts". You can play "extinction" later.

9
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:24,200
Okay. Come on, guys.

10
00:04:25,620 --> 00:04:27,500
So, where's Eddie?

11
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:31,500
He said something about being on a
verge of an evolutionary breakthrough.

12
00:04:31,590 --> 00:04:32,920
Really?

13
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:36,760
I'm flying!

14
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:39,590
Some breakthrough.

15
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:46,140
Look out!
You're going the wrong way. Crazy mammoth.

16
00:04:52,810 --> 00:04:55,320
Hey, do the world a favour!

17
00:04:55,570 --> 00:04:58,400
Move your issues off the road!

18
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:02,910
If my trunk was that small,
I wouldn't draw attention to myself, pal.

19
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,330
Give me a break.

20
00:05:04,410 --> 00:05:06,950
We've been waddlin' all day.

21
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:11,380
Oh, go ahead. Follow the crowd.

22
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:13,210
It'll be quieter when you're gone.

23
00:05:14,630 --> 00:05:18,500
Come on. If he wants to freeze to death, let him.

24
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:28,930
Hey, hey. I'm up, I'm up!

25
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:34,690
Hey, rise and shine, everybody.

26
00:05:35,230 --> 00:05:37,730
Huh? Zak? Marshall?

27
00:05:37,990 --> 00:05:41,110
Bertie? Uncle Fungus?

28
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:42,780
Where is everybody?

29
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:45,120
Come on, guys.
We gonna miss the mi.. the mi.. the...

30
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:47,740
...migration.

31
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,960
They left without me.

32
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,960
They do this every year!

33
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:59,630
Why? Doesn't anyone love me?

34
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:04,390
Isn't there anyone who cares about Sid the Sloth?

35
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,810
All right, I'll just go by myself.

36
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,850
Oh! Sick!

37
00:06:13,150 --> 00:06:15,940
Hey, wide body! Kerb it next time!

38
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:18,400
Oh! Jeez... Oh..Yuck! Oh..

39
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:21,740
I can't believe it. Fresh wild greens.

40
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:24,660
Frank, where did you ever...

41
00:06:24,740 --> 00:06:26,700
Go ahead, dig in.

42
00:06:26,490 --> 00:06:29,490
A dandelion.
I thought the frost wiped them all out.

43
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:31,200
All but one.

44
00:06:33,330 --> 00:06:35,000
Makes me so... I wanna..

45
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,750
Oh! Yuck!

46
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:41,900
This has definitely not been my day.
I mean... You know what I'm saying, buddy?

47
00:06:41,510 --> 00:06:42,840
Oh, what a mess.

48
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,640
Hey, you rhinos, you know, you have really
tiny brains, did you know that?

49
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,680
No. It's just a fact.

50
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:47,890
No offence!

51
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:49,890
But you barely know what I'm talking about.

52
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:52,600
Oh, Yummo.

53
00:06:52,730 --> 00:06:54,350
A dandelion.

54
00:06:54,390 --> 00:06:56,400
Must be the last one of the season.

55
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:01,490
Carl.
Easy, Frank.

56
00:07:01,610 --> 00:07:03,320
He ruined our salad.

57
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:07,740
Oh, my mistake.
That was my mistake. Let me...

58
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:09,910
No, seriously, let me take care of this.

59
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:12,000
Oh. What is this?

60
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,870
Pine cones!!!

61
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:15,960
Oh my goodness, they're my favourite.

62
00:07:16,750 --> 00:07:18,250
Hmm, delicious.

63
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:19,000
Ow.

64
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:22,460
That's a... good eating.

65
00:07:22,590 --> 00:07:25,840
Don't let me hog them all up.
No, here, you have some.

66
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:27,100
Tasty, isn't it?

67
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:28,680
Bon appГ©tit.

68
00:07:29,930 --> 00:07:30,900
Now?

69
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,350
Now.

70
00:07:39,590 --> 00:07:40,480
Hey!

71
00:07:43,490 --> 00:07:44,900
Just pretend that I am not here.

72
00:07:45,990 --> 00:07:47,610
I wanna hit him at full speed.

73
00:07:47,660 --> 00:07:50,280
That's okay, Frank.
We'll have some fun with him.

74
00:07:50,410 --> 00:07:52,910
Don't let them impale me, please.
I wanna live!

75
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:53,950
Get off me!

76
00:07:54,330 --> 00:07:56,460
Come on, you're making a scene.

77
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:59,460
We'll just take our furry pinata and go.
Would you mind?

78
00:07:59,630 --> 00:08:02,590
Hey. Buddy, if it's not them today,
it's just someone else tomorrow.

79
00:08:02,670 --> 00:08:05,260
I like rather not be today. Okay?

80
00:08:05,670 --> 00:08:08,640
Look. We're gonnaa break your neck so you
don't feel a thing. How's that?

81
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:11,680
Wait a minute.
I thought rhinos were vegetarians.

82
00:08:11,890 --> 00:08:13,850
An excelent point.
Shut up!

83
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:16,690
Who says we gonna eat him
after we kill him?

84
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:17,560
Yeh, come on, move it.

85
00:08:17,690 --> 00:08:20,690
You know, I don't like
animals that kill for pleasure.

86
00:08:20,770 --> 00:08:22,190
Save it for a mammal that cares.

87
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:24,230
I'm a mammal that cares.

88
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:26,190
Okay, look. If either of you make it

89
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:29,490
across that sink hole in front of you, you get the Sloth.

90
00:08:29,530 --> 00:08:32,780
That's right, you losers.
You take one step and you're dead.

91
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:41,290
You were bluffing, huh?
Yeah, that was a bluff.

92
00:08:42,250 --> 00:08:42,960
Get him!

93
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:22,210
A dandelion?

94
00:09:25,250 --> 00:09:26,250
We did it!

95
00:09:27,550 --> 00:09:28,550
What?

96
00:09:35,510 --> 00:09:37,310
You have beautiful eyes.

97
00:09:37,430 --> 00:09:39,270
Get off my face.

98
00:09:39,850 --> 00:09:43,310
Wow, you and me, we make a great team.

99
00:09:43,310 --> 00:09:44,820
I mean. What'd you say we just head South together?

100
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:47,320
Great!
Yeah, hey jump up on my back and relax your whole way.

101
00:09:47,730 --> 00:09:49,280
Wow. Really?
No.

102
00:09:49,570 --> 00:09:51,280
Wait, aren't you going to South?

103
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:53,700
The changing seasons, migration instincts?

104
00:09:53,950 --> 00:09:56,580
Any of this a-ringin' a bell?
I guess not, bye.

105
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:59,540
Okay, then thanks for the help.
I can take it from here.

106
00:10:00,830 --> 00:10:04,540
Hey, you over-grown weasel.
Wait till we get down there.

107
00:10:05,420 --> 00:10:08,950
Ohohou. That south thing is way overrated.
The heat, the crowd. Who needs any?

108
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:13,630
Isn't this great? You and me, two bachelors
knockin' about in the wild.

109
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:17,560
No, you just want a bodyguard
so you don't become somebody's side dish.

110
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:20,100
You're very shrewd mammal.

111
00:10:20,230 --> 00:10:23,150
Can you lead the way, Mr. Big Guy?
Didn't get the name.

112
00:10:23,230 --> 00:10:25,200
Manfred.
Manfred? Yuck.

113
00:10:25,190 --> 00:10:29,530
How about Manny the Moody Mammoth?
Or Manny the Melancholy... Manny the...

114
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,780
Stop following me.

115
00:10:36,950 --> 00:10:40,000
OK, so you've got issues.
Look, you won't even know I'm here.

116
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:41,960
I'll just zip the lip when I say...

117
00:11:27,130 --> 00:11:31,250
Look at the cute little baby, Diego.

118
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:36,100
Isn't it nice if he'll be joining us for breakfast?

119
00:11:36,220 --> 00:11:38,430
It wouldn't be breakfast without him.

120
00:11:38,640 --> 00:11:44,390
Especially since his daddy wiped out half
our pack and wears our skin to keep warm.

121
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:47,560
An eye for an eye. Don't you think?

122
00:11:47,730 --> 00:11:51,230
Let's show that human what happens
when he messes with Sabers.

123
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:54,400
Alert the troops. We attack at dawn.

124
00:11:55,610 --> 00:12:00,240
And Diego, bring me that baby. Alive.

125
00:12:00,330 --> 00:12:05,500
If I'm gonna enjoy my revenge, I want it to be fresh.

126
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,150
Phew. I'm wiped out.

127
00:12:29,400 --> 00:12:30,610
That's your shelter?

128
00:12:30,810 --> 00:12:34,300
Hey. You're a big guy. You got a lot of wood.
I'm a little guy.

129
00:12:34,230 --> 00:12:35,440
You've got half a stick.

130
00:12:35,570 --> 00:12:40,200
Yeah, but with my little stick, and my highly evolved brain...

131
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:42,280
I shall create fire.

132
00:12:42,830 --> 00:12:44,400
Fascinating.

133
00:12:44,910 --> 00:12:49,370
We'll see if brains triumph over brawn tonight.
Now, won't we?

134
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:56,760
Hey, I think I saw spark.

135
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:04,680
Any chance I can squeeze in there with you Manny?
Old pal?

136
00:13:04,890 --> 00:13:07,230
Isn't there someone else you can annoy?

137
00:13:07,430 --> 00:13:11,360
Friends? Family? Poisonous reptiles?

138
00:13:11,360 --> 00:13:15,530
My family abandoned me. They just kinda migrated without me.

139
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:17,990
You should see what they did last year.

140
00:13:18,610 --> 00:13:22,700
You know, I mean. They woke up early and
finely tied my hands and feet.

141
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:28,540
and they gagged me with a fieldmouse, barricaded the cave door,
and covered their tracks, went through water so l'd lose their scent,

142
00:13:28,710 --> 00:13:31,250
and... who needs 'em, anyway?

143
00:13:35,630 --> 00:13:37,840
So what about you? You've family?

144
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:45,260
Okay, you're tired, I see.
Well, we'll talk more in the morning.

145
00:13:45,390 --> 00:13:47,640
Ow, ow, a, a, ow, ow.

146
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:49,480
Manfred? Manfred.

147
00:13:49,890 --> 00:13:51,100
Could you scooch over a drop?

148
00:13:52,650 --> 00:13:54,940
Come on, nobody falls asleep that fast.

149
00:13:55,610 --> 00:13:56,900
Manny!

150
00:16:48,610 --> 00:16:50,620
There's Diego, fall back!

151
00:16:57,290 --> 00:16:58,580
Where's the baby?

152
00:16:58,710 --> 00:17:01,750
I've lost it over the falls.
You lost it?

153
00:17:05,840 --> 00:17:08,180
I want that baby, Diego.
I'll get it.

154
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:12,300
You'd better. Unless you want to serve
yourself as the replacement.

155
00:17:12,430 --> 00:17:15,720
We'll go up to Half peak. Meet us there.

156
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:18,640
It'd better be alive.

157
00:17:20,310 --> 00:17:22,810
Can we trust you with that, Diego?

158
00:17:23,110 --> 00:17:24,200
Let's go!

159
00:17:48,340 --> 00:17:50,590
and then she picked this hair off my shoulder and says, look...

160
00:17:50,610 --> 00:17:52,300
If you're gonna have an extra mating dance,

161
00:17:52,390 --> 00:17:54,930
at least pick a female with the same color pelt, right?

162
00:17:54,930 --> 00:17:58,310
And I thought, wow, she's gonna go praying mantis on me.
I mean, you know what I'm saying?

163
00:17:58,310 --> 00:18:01,200
If you find a mate in life, you should be loyal.

164
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:03,360
In your case, grateful.
Get away from me.

165
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:08,360
Well, I think mating for life is stupid.
I mean there's plenty of Sid to go around.

166
00:18:09,490 --> 00:18:11,700
Manny?

167
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:10,300
Look at that.
He's okay.

168
00:19:21,770 --> 00:19:23,520
She's gone.

169
00:19:33,900 --> 00:19:36,450
Hey, hey, hey Manny, are you forgetting something?

170
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:39,300
No.
But you just saved him.

171
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:42,160
Yeah, but I'm still trying to get rid of the last thing I saved.

172
00:19:42,250 --> 00:19:44,160
You can't leave him here.

173
00:19:48,670 --> 00:19:50,210
Look, there's smoke.

174
00:19:50,250 --> 00:19:53,380
That's his herd right up the hill. We should return him.

175
00:19:53,590 --> 00:19:56,300
Let's get something straight here. Okay?
There's no "we".

176
00:19:56,510 --> 00:19:58,300
There never was a "we".

177
00:19:58,430 --> 00:20:01,850
In fact, without me, there wouldn't even be a "you"!

178
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,350
Just up the hill.

179
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:10,200
Listen very carefully. I'm not g-o-i-n-g.

180
00:20:10,190 --> 00:20:11,690
Fine. Be a jerk.

181
00:20:12,150 --> 00:20:13,240
I'll take care of him.

182
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:14,860
Go. Yeah, that's good.

183
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,610
You'll take care...
You can't even take care of yourself.

184
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:18,700
This I gotta see.

185
00:20:18,820 --> 00:20:22,870
I'll return you. We don't need that meany-weeny mammoth, do we?

186
00:20:22,910 --> 00:20:24,500
No, we don't.

187
00:20:54,530 --> 00:20:57,740
You're the embarrassment to nature, do you know that?

188
00:20:58,450 --> 00:20:59,820
That is cake.

189
00:20:59,870 --> 00:21:01,910
I'm fine. I'm fine!

190
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:03,450
I'm gonna die.

191
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:34,190
That pink thing is mine.

192
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:36,610
No, actually that pink thing belongs to us.

193
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:43,240
Us? You two are a bit of an odd couple.

194
00:21:43,370 --> 00:21:45,990
There is no "us".
I see.

195
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,290
Can't have one of your own, so you want to adopt.

196
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:50,670
Look, I'm sorry to interrupt this snack.

197
00:21:50,670 --> 00:21:51,880
But we gotta go.

198
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:53,790
The baby, please.

199
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:55,300
I was returning him to his herd.

200
00:21:55,380 --> 00:21:57,710
Oh, yeah. Nice try, bucktooth.

201
00:21:57,760 --> 00:21:59,800
You're calling me a liar?
I didn't say that.

202
00:21:59,930 --> 00:22:01,510
You were thinking it.

203
00:22:01,930 --> 00:22:04,430
I don't like this cat. He reads minds.

204
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:06,770
Name is Diego, friend.

205
00:22:06,810 --> 00:22:08,640
Manfred. And I'm not your friend.

206
00:22:08,850 --> 00:22:11,770
Fine, Manfred.

207
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:14,650
If you're looking for the humans, you're wasting your time.

208
00:22:14,860 --> 00:22:16,700
They left this morning.

209
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:19,110
Thanks for the advice. Now beat it.

210
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:21,360
All right, I'll help you bring it to its herd.

211
00:22:21,490 --> 00:22:23,490
But promise me that you leave me alone after that.

212
00:22:23,570 --> 00:22:25,200
Okay, okay, deal.

213
00:22:25,370 --> 00:22:26,990
What's your problem?
You're my problem.

214
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:29,450
But I think you're stressed.
That's why you eat so much.

215
00:22:29,620 --> 00:22:31,580
I mean. It's hard to get fat on a vegan diet.

216
00:22:31,670 --> 00:22:35,790
I'm not fat. It's all that fur.
It makes me look pooffy.

217
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:39,460
All right, you have fat hair.
But when you're ready to talk, I'm here.

218
00:22:43,900 --> 00:22:44,890
I don't know. Just drop it on the ledge.

219
00:22:46,810 --> 00:22:48,970
Shouldn't we make sure they found him?
Good idea.

220
00:22:49,140 --> 00:22:50,640
No, no, no!
Wait. Wait.

221
00:22:52,140 --> 00:22:54,440
Don't spear me!

222
00:22:57,900 --> 00:22:59,320
Ohhhm. This is a problem.

223
00:22:59,400 --> 00:23:00,860
Now what?

224
00:23:02,300 --> 00:23:03,740
Oh. That's perfect.

225
00:23:34,230 --> 00:23:35,650
I told you they were gone.

226
00:23:35,770 --> 00:23:36,860
Look who it is.

227
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:39,610
Don't you have some poor defenseless animals to disembowel?

228
00:23:39,690 --> 00:23:42,300
They couldn't be far. I mean. They went this way?

229
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:43,780
Or this way?

230
00:23:43,990 --> 00:23:46,300
You don't know much about tracking, do you?

231
00:23:46,110 --> 00:23:49,910
Hey, I'm a Sloth. I see a tree, eat a leaf, that's my tracking.

232
00:23:50,330 --> 00:23:52,160
You didn't miss them by much.

233
00:23:52,370 --> 00:23:53,910
It's still green.

234
00:23:54,210 --> 00:23:55,960
They headed north 2 hours ago.

235
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:58,170
It's still green. They headed north 2 hours ago.

236
00:24:02,460 --> 00:24:04,880
You don't need this aggravation.

237
00:24:06,180 --> 00:24:07,680
Give me the baby.

238
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:10,140
I can track humans a lot faster than you can.

239
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:12,890
And you're just a good citizen helping out, right?

240
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:14,980
I just know where the humans are going.

241
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:16,600
Glacier-pass.

242
00:24:16,730 --> 00:24:19,980
Everybody knows they have a settlement on the other side.

243
00:24:21,190 --> 00:24:23,700
Well, unless you know how to track,

244
00:24:23,150 --> 00:24:26,200
you've never gonna reach them before the pass closes up with snow.

245
00:24:26,410 --> 00:24:29,700
Which should be like, tomorrow.

246
00:24:29,320 --> 00:24:33,500
So you can give that baby to me or go get lost in the blizzard.

247
00:24:33,540 --> 00:24:35,800
It's your choice.

248
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:45,800
Here's your little bundle of joy.
We'll return it to the humans.

249
00:24:46,550 --> 00:24:51,810
Oooh. The Big Bad Tigey Wigey get left behind.
Poor Tigey Wigey...

250
00:24:51,930 --> 00:24:55,560
