00:49:13,870 --> 00:49:15,240
Looks just like you.

511
00:49:15,370 --> 00:49:17,750
Oh, he's got a family.

512
00:49:17,870 --> 00:49:20,370
Oh, he's happy.

513
00:49:20,500 --> 00:49:21,920
Look he is playing with his kid.

514
00:49:22,800 --> 00:49:24,000
See Manny that's your problem.

515
00:49:24,170 --> 00:49:25,750
That's what mammoths supposed to do.

516
00:49:25,960 --> 00:49:28,100
Sid.
Find a she-mmoth, have the little baby mammoth...

517
00:49:28,340 --> 00:49:30,680
Sid!
What?

518
00:49:30,720 --> 00:49:32,900
Shut up!

519
00:52:59,840 --> 00:53:02,550
Well. Would you look at that.

520
00:53:02,680 --> 00:53:05,310
The tiger actually did it. There's Half-peak.

521
00:53:05,430 --> 00:53:06,850
Next stop. Glacier pass.

522
00:53:09,600 --> 00:53:10,900
How could I ever have doubted you?

523
00:53:11,190 --> 00:53:13,110
Did you hear that little fella?

524
00:53:13,190 --> 00:53:14,900
You are almost home?

525
00:53:19,480 --> 00:53:20,690
My feet are sweating.

526
00:53:20,690 --> 00:53:23,610
Do we have to get a news flash
every time your body does something?

527
00:53:23,820 --> 00:53:25,280
Don't pay attention. Just ignore him

528
00:53:25,440 --> 00:53:28,610
Seriously, my feet are really hot...

529
00:53:33,740 --> 00:53:37,160
Tell me that was your stomach.

530
00:53:37,160 --> 00:53:38,920
I am sure it was just thunder.

531
00:53:39,120 --> 00:53:42,380
From under.., ground?

532
00:54:02,400 --> 00:54:04,900
Come on keep up with me.

533
00:54:04,900 --> 00:54:06,860
I would if you were moving.

534
00:54:09,860 --> 00:54:11,660
Wow. I wish I could jump like that.

535
00:54:11,780 --> 00:54:13,870
Wish granted.

536
00:54:17,620 --> 00:54:18,960
Come on move faster.

537
00:54:19,800 --> 00:54:21,710
Have you noticed the river of lava?

538
00:54:41,200 --> 00:54:42,230
Hold Pinky!

539
00:55:14,640 --> 00:55:16,220
Manny!!!

540
00:55:28,320 --> 00:55:30,570
Manny, Manny, Manny are you ok?

541
00:55:30,570 --> 00:55:32,610
Come on, come on  say something.
Anything!

542
00:55:35,450 --> 00:55:38,410
What. What? I can't hear you.

543
00:55:38,580 --> 00:55:40,700
You are standing on my trunk.

544
00:55:41,250 --> 00:55:43,000
Are you OK?

545
00:55:43,960 --> 00:55:44,880
Why did you do that ?

546
00:55:44,960 --> 00:55:47,340
You could have die trying to save me.

547
00:55:47,790 --> 00:55:50,630
That's what you do in a herd...

548
00:55:50,920 --> 00:55:52,970
We look out for each other.

549
00:55:53,680 --> 00:55:55,800
Well... thanks.

550
00:55:57,300 --> 00:56:00,200
I don't now how about you guys, but...

551
00:56:00,140 --> 00:56:02,930
we're the weirdest herd I've ever seen.

552
00:56:20,660 --> 00:56:23,710
I can't wait to get my claws in that mammoth.

553
00:56:23,750 --> 00:56:28,170
No one touches the mammoth until I get that baby.

554
00:56:30,750 --> 00:56:36,300
First, I'm gonna slice its hind quarters into sections.
I'm on to put the white meat in one pile and dark in ano...

555
00:56:36,300 --> 00:56:38,390
Hey. Knock it off. I am starving.

556
00:56:38,510 --> 00:56:42,560
Next, the shoulders. Occasionally tough, but extremely juicy.

557
00:56:42,560 --> 00:56:44,100
I told you to knock it off!

558
00:56:44,140 --> 00:56:45,940
Save your energy!

559
00:56:46,600 --> 00:56:47,270
Mammoths don't go down easy.

560
00:56:47,900 --> 00:56:50,730
There is only one way to do it.

561
00:56:50,940 --> 00:56:53,320
First you have to force it into a corner.

562
00:56:53,990 --> 00:56:56,660
Cut off his retreat.

563
00:56:57,200 --> 00:56:58,910
And when you three have it trapped...

564
00:56:59,300 --> 00:57:00,910
I'll go for the throat.

565
00:57:11,900 --> 00:57:13,800
Guys. We gotta get this kid out of the wind.

566
00:57:17,880 --> 00:57:20,220
How much further? 3 miles.

567
00:57:22,180 --> 00:57:23,850
I'm beat. We'll get there in the morning.

568
00:57:26,230 --> 00:57:28,140
What're you doing?

569
00:57:28,190 --> 00:57:30,110
I'm putting sloth on the map.

570
00:57:33,230 --> 00:57:36,490
Hey. Why don't you make it realistic and draw him lying down?

571
00:57:36,860 --> 00:57:39,490
And make him rounder.

572
00:57:40,950 --> 00:57:41,780
Perfect.

573
00:57:43,540 --> 00:57:45,160
I forgot how to laugh.

574
00:57:52,130 --> 00:57:53,550
I am a genius.

575
00:57:58,900 --> 00:57:59,840
From now one you'll have to refer to me as...

576
00:58:00,220 --> 00:58:02,470
Sid, Lord of the flame.

577
00:58:02,550 --> 00:58:06,850
Hey, Lord of the flame, your tail's on fire.

578
00:58:14,730 --> 00:58:15,360
Thank you.

579
00:58:15,480 --> 00:58:18,700
From now one I'm gonna call you Diego.

580
00:58:18,900 --> 00:58:21,620
Lord you've touched me and you are dead.

581
00:58:21,870 --> 00:58:24,240
I am just kidding you little knuckle-head.

582
00:58:24,490 --> 00:58:27,500
Hey lovebirds. Look at this.

583
00:58:33,800 --> 00:58:34,960
I don't believe it.

584
00:58:48,850 --> 00:58:52,810
Come here, you little biped.
Come here, you little wormy-worm.

585
00:58:53,520 --> 00:58:55,730
Come to uncle Sid.

586
00:58:55,860 --> 00:58:58,110
No no this way, this way.

587
00:59:00,200 --> 00:59:04,780
No. no, no. Go to him. Go to him.

588
00:59:07,490 --> 00:59:10,400
Ok...

589
00:59:11,160 --> 00:59:12,800
Good job.

590
00:59:13,540 --> 00:59:15,460
Keep practicing.

591
00:59:17,710 --> 00:59:21,260
Look at that. Our little guy is growing up.

592
00:59:23,510 --> 00:59:26,600
Come on. Sleep time, lumpy.

593
00:59:31,930 --> 00:59:33,750
Look at that big pushover.

594
00:59:35,610 --> 00:59:39,400
You know Diego, I've never had a friend
who'd risk his life for me.

595
00:59:40,700 --> 00:59:44,570
Yeah, Manny's... is a good guy.

596
00:59:44,740 --> 00:59:47,530
Yeah he is.

597
00:59:47,980 --> 00:59:50,190
Well, good night

598
01:00:22,360 --> 01:00:24,450
All right. Let's get you all cleaned up.

599
01:00:24,570 --> 01:00:29,300
I mean what's your daddy gonna say when
we go back smudgy and stinky like this?

600
01:00:29,160 --> 01:00:30,700
OK. Let me just clean that up.

601
01:00:30,830 --> 01:00:32,790
That looks good and little bit here...

602
01:00:32,910 --> 01:00:35,800
You clean up nice - little fellow.

603
01:00:35,210 --> 01:00:38,210
I think he start to look like me.
Hey Diego, what do you say?

604
01:00:40,500 --> 01:00:41,960
Maybe we shouldn't do this.

605
01:00:42,900 --> 01:00:43,100
Why not?

606
01:00:43,130 --> 01:00:45,300
Because if we save him, he'll grow up to be a hunter.

607
01:00:45,430 --> 01:00:47,180
And who do you think he'll hunt?

608
01:00:47,300 --> 01:00:49,390
Maybe because we save him he won't hunt us.
Ow!

609
01:00:49,510 --> 01:00:54,480
Yeh, maybe he'll grow fur and a long
skinny neck and call you mamma!

610
01:00:54,890 --> 01:00:56,560
What is your problem?

611
01:00:56,980 --> 01:01:00,110
Nothing. Lets go, it's freezing my tail off.

612
01:01:19,170 --> 01:01:21,800
Hey Diego, you've frozen back there?

613
01:01:25,760 --> 01:01:27,430
Get down.
What?

614
01:01:27,840 --> 01:01:29,510
Shhh!
Get down and follow me.

615
01:01:29,510 --> 01:01:30,550
Hey, hey! What's going on?

616
01:01:30,680 --> 01:01:35,270
At the bottom of Half-peak...
there is an ambush waiting for you.

617
01:01:35,730 --> 01:01:37,850
What?
What do you mean ambush.

618
01:01:39,940 --> 01:01:41,190
You set us up?

619
01:01:41,190 --> 01:01:43,900
It was my job, I was supposed to get the baby but then...

620
01:01:43,900 --> 01:01:45,650
You brought us home for dinner!!!

621
01:01:46,700 --> 01:01:47,860
That's it, you're out of the herd.

622
01:01:47,860 --> 01:01:48,700
I am sorry.

623
01:01:48,780 --> 01:01:51,120
No you are not. Not yet.

624
01:01:51,280 --> 01:01:52,660
Listen, I can help you.

625
01:01:52,870 --> 01:01:53,910
Stay close Sid.

626
01:01:53,950 --> 01:01:55,160
We can fight our way out.

627
01:01:55,160 --> 01:01:57,400
You can't. Pack's too strong.

628
01:01:57,500 --> 01:01:58,290
You have to trust me!

629
01:01:58,290 --> 01:02:00,630
Trust you ? Why in the world would we trust you ?

630
01:02:00,710 --> 01:02:03,920
Because I am your only chance.

631
01:02:17,600 --> 01:02:18,310
Hello ladies!

632
01:02:19,810 --> 01:02:21,810
Hey look who decided to show up.

633
01:02:22,690 --> 01:02:24,820
Diego. I was beginning to worry about you.

634
01:02:25,820 --> 01:02:26,650
No need to worry.

635
01:02:26,860 --> 01:02:32,700
In about 2 minutes you'll be satisfying your taste...
for revenge.

636
01:02:32,200 --> 01:02:33,280
Very nice!

637
01:02:33,950 --> 01:02:35,410
I see the sloth!

638
01:02:35,490 --> 01:02:37,500
And he's got the baby!

639
01:02:37,500 --> 01:02:40,210
Don't give away your positions until we see the mammoth.

640
01:02:40,420 --> 01:02:42,210
He's the one we have to surprise.

641
01:02:43,960 --> 01:02:46,500
You wanna maul something. Don't you think?

642
01:02:46,170 --> 01:02:47,800
I wanna maul.

643
01:02:48,630 --> 01:02:50,430
Then what are you waiting for?

644
01:02:53,500 --> 01:02:54,800
No, I said wait for the mammoth!

645
01:03:17,830 --> 01:03:19,200
Yohou! Backscratcher. Ahaa!

646
01:03:19,410 --> 01:03:20,460
Eat my powder!

647
01:03:39,400 --> 01:03:41,940
Loop-de-loop. Slalom, slalom baby!

648
01:04:07,590 --> 01:04:11,550
Sorry fellas, it got a little frostbite.

649
01:04:12,590 --> 01:04:13,840
Get him!

650
01:04:18,430 --> 01:04:20,100
Surprise!

651
01:04:24,900 --> 01:04:26,770
Ok, follow me.

652
01:04:26,860 --> 01:04:29,270
We'll pick up Sid and get outta here while we can.

653
01:04:29,900 --> 01:04:34,280
Come on Diego, let's bring this mammoth down.

654
01:04:45,960 --> 01:04:47,630
There he is.

655
01:04:50,340 --> 01:04:53,500
That's right - where's the baby. Oh!

656
01:04:56,590 --> 01:05:03,270
Survival of the fittest. I don't think so. Yeah!

657
01:05:14,110 --> 01:05:15,240
What are you doing?

658
01:05:15,320 --> 01:05:18,570
Leave the mammoth alone!

659
01:05:21,620 --> 01:05:24,750
Fine! I'll take you down first.

660
01:06:40,660 --> 01:06:41,910
We did it!

661
01:06:54,710 --> 01:06:57,960
We were some team, huh?

662
01:06:59,220 --> 01:07:02,340
Were? Come on. We're still a team.

663
01:07:02,970 --> 01:07:05,260
I am sorry I set you up.

664
01:07:05,470 --> 01:07:08,600
Ah. You know me. I'm too lazy to hold a grudge.

665
01:07:11,940 --> 01:07:13,610
Hey. Knock it off, squirt.

666
01:07:15,700 --> 01:07:16,110
You have to be strong.

667
01:07:16,940 --> 01:07:20,280
You have to take care of Manfred and Sid.

668
01:07:21,530 --> 01:07:22,990
Especially Sid.

669
01:07:23,820 --> 01:07:30,710
Come on. You can lick this. You're a tiger.
Look I'll carry you. Come on, what do you say?

670
01:07:30,830 --> 01:07:33,210
Come on Diego, come on.

671
01:07:33,330 --> 01:07:36,130
Tell him he's going to be OK, Manny.

672
01:07:36,960 --> 01:07:40,300
Listen. You have to leave me here.

673
01:07:40,720 --> 01:07:45,510
If those humans get through the pass, you'll never catch them.

674
01:07:45,850 --> 01:07:47,180
You didn't have to do that.

675
01:07:49,600 --> 01:07:51,350
That's what you do in a herd.

676
01:11:07,340 --> 01:11:10,720
Don't forget about us, ok?

677
01:11:13,800 --> 01:11:15,680
We won't forget about you.

678
01:11:56,180 --> 01:11:57,600
Good bye.

679
01:11:58,890 --> 01:12:01,600
Good bye. Good bye.

680
01:12:01,770 --> 01:12:02,440
Sid.

681
01:12:02,560 --> 01:12:04,690
Good bye.

682
01:12:10,110 --> 01:12:12,650
That's right. Where is the baby?

683
01:12:12,780 --> 01:12:13,700
Come on Sid.

684
01:12:13,820 --> 01:12:15,530
Let's head South.

685
01:12:36,430 --> 01:12:39,760
Save your breath Sid. You know humans can't talk.

686
01:12:40,140 --> 01:12:41,390
Diego?

687
01:12:41,560 --> 01:12:42,810
You're Ok!

688
01:12:42,850 --> 01:12:44,440
9 lives baby.

689
01:12:44,900 --> 01:12:46,980
You're ok. You're ok.

690
01:12:48,610 --> 01:12:50,610
I could kiss ya. m. m. m. m. m. m. m. m. m.

691
01:12:50,690 --> 01:12:52,490
Yuck, yuck. Bleeh.

692
01:12:52,570 --> 01:12:54,780
Welcome back partner. Want a lift?

693
01:12:54,910 --> 01:12:57,700
No thanks. I've got to save whatever dignity I've got left.

694
01:12:57,820 --> 01:13:01,450
You're hanging out with us now, buddy.
Dignity's got nothing to do with it.

695
01:13:01,450 --> 01:13:02,700
But I'll take that lift.

696
01:13:02,700 --> 01:13:04,210
Yeh. Climb aboard.
Pick me up, buddy.

697
01:13:05,000 --> 01:13:06,460
Mush!

698
01:13:07,290 --> 01:13:09,790
Or not mush, either way.

699
01:13:12,710 --> 01:13:20,100
This gonna be the best migration ever. I'm telling you.
I'll show you all my favourite watering holes.
I turn brown when the fungus in my fur dries.

700
01:13:20,100 --> 01:13:21,720
Sounds very attractive!

701
01:13:21,810 --> 01:13:27,100
You know. This whole Ice age thing's getting old.
You know what l could go for? Global warming!

702
01:13:27,190 --> 01:13:27,690
Aye.

703
01:13:27,810 --> 01:13:28,940
Keep dreamin'.

704
01:13:29,200 --> 01:13:29,610
No, really!

